|t=So he goes forth to the sky among the stars, among the circumpolar stars, with Pepi’s '''striking-power''' atop him, his viciousness at his sides, and his magic at his feet.}}

====Usage notes====
Sometimes used in parallel to {{m|egy|pḥtj||strength}}. In other passages it appears in an exactly parallel context to {{m|egy|bꜣw||[[ba]]-power, might and glory}}: compare PT 474 against PT 306 in the Pyramid Texts.

While Erman and Grapow take this word to mean ‘head ornament’ in some passages, Gardiner convincingly argues that this is a misinterpretation, the true sense being ‘readiness to strike’ throughout. Gardiner also proposes that the ‘moment, time’ sense of {{m|egy||ꜣt}} is not independent, but developed from the ‘readiness to strike’ sense by way of reference to the suddenness or speed of a strike. Allen instead takes the ‘moment’ meaning as primary, rendering the ‘readiness to strike’ sense as ‘moment of rage’.

