bn:
===Etymology===
Related to (and probably developed from) earlier {{m|egy|nn||not}}.<ref>Oréal, Elsa (2022) “The negative existential cycle in Ancient Egyptian” in Ljuba Veselinova & Arja Hamari (eds.), ''The Negative Existential Cycle'', Berlin: Language Science Press, pages 197–230</ref> The spelling with {{m|egy||b-}} may reflect a graphic phenomenon rather than a sound change. Compare the Late Egyptian development of {{m|egy|bw}} from Earlier Egyptian {{m|egy|nj}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-pr}}

===Particle===
{{egy-part|proclitic|head=b:n}}

# {{lb|egy|Late Egyptian}} [[not]]; {{ng|negates the adverbial sentence/first present, the third future, and the optative}}
# {{lb|egy|Late Egyptian}} [[not]]; {{ng|negates a nominal sentence}}
# {{lb|egy|Late Egyptian|with a following noun or pronoun}} [[without]]; there not being any …

====Usage notes====
The negative constructions with this particle are isomorphic to the corresponding positive constructions without it; they are formed by simply prepending {{m|egy||bn}} to the start of the clause. In the negated adverbial and nominal sentences, occasionally another negation particle, {{m|egy|jwnꜣ}}, is used with {{m|egy||bn}}, discontinuously following the negated element. In higher linguistic registers {{m|egy|nn||not}} is sometimes used instead of {{m|egy||bn}}.

===References===
* {{R:egy:Junge|113, 115, 117, 123–124, 140, 169–170}}
