Unclear. Presumably consisting of the unattested root ''*ꜥbr'' with [[prefix]] ''m-''. 

Semantically, this word might have originally referred to a “[[lunar month]] of thirty days” as suggested by A. Ember (1926); cf. {{ncog|jbn|u-yěr||moon; thirty}}. Based on this, Takacs (2007) compares the root ''*ꜥbr'' ~ ''*ꜥrb'' (via [[metathesis]]) to Proto-Agaw ''*ʔärb-'' ~ ''ʔärf-'' ("moon"), and further to {{der|egy|sem-pro|*ʕ-r-p|t=cloud}} (whence {{cog|he|ערפל}}).<ref>{{R:egy:EDE|v=3|p=176}}</ref>

