nf:
===Pronunciation===
{{egy-pr}}

===Pronoun===
{{egy-pron|dem|deictic=distal|head=n:f}}

# [[that]]

====Usage notes====
This demonstrative is a pronoun, and so does not directly modify nouns. In Middle Egyptian it becomes used as a demonstrative for plural nouns in place of the old adjectives {{m|egy|jpf}} and {{m|egy|jptf}}. When used in this way, it precedes the noun, with the genitival adjective {{m|egy|nj|n(j)}} in between, e.g. "those feet" is {{m|egy||nf n(j) rdw}} (literally "that of feet").

It forms a contrastive pair with the demonstrative pronoun {{m|egy|nn}}, in which {{m|egy||nf}} is [[distal]].

