#* {{Q|egy||ShS.|lines 149–150|quote={{egy-h|aHa-a:n-s-b-t:bH-A2-n:f-i-m-A1-m-M22-M22-D:d-n:A1-m-n:f-nDs-m-ib-Z1-f-!-D:d-<!--150-->f:n-A1-D35-wr-r-n:k\-a:n-tyw-W23:Z2ss-xpr-r:*t-nb-nTr-sn-n:t-r-tr-N33C:Z2ss}}
|tr=ꜥḥꜥ.n sbt.n.f jm.j m '''nn''' ḏd.n.j m nf m jb.f ḏd.f n.j (j)n wr n.k ꜥntjw ḫpr.t(j) ⟨m⟩ nb sntr
|t=Then he laughed at me – and at '''this''' that I’d said – as being wrong to his mind, saying to me: Are you abundant in myrrh, turned into a lord of incense?<ref>Or ‘You aren’t abundant in myrrh …’, if the initial particle is read as negative {{m|egy|nj}} instead of interrogative {{m|egy|jn}}. The expected negative particle for such a clause would be {{m|egy|nn}}, so an interrogative is more plausible. For a detailed discussion see Scalf, Foy (2009) “Is That a Rhetorical Question? Shipwrecked Sailor (pHermitage 1115) 150 Reconsidered” in ''Zeitschrift für Ägyptische Sprache und Altertumskunde'', volume 136, issue 2, pages 155–159.</ref>}}

=====Usage notes=====
This demonstrative is a pronoun, and so does not directly modify nouns. In Middle Egyptian it becomes used as a demonstrative for plural nouns in place of the old adjectives {{m|egy|jpn}} and {{m|egy|jptn}}. When used in this way, it precedes the noun, with the genitival adjective {{m|egy|nj|n(j)}} in between, e.g. "these feet" is {{m|egy||nn n(j) rdw}} (literally "this of feet").

It forms a contrastive pair with the demonstrative pronoun {{m|egy|nf}}, in which {{m|egy||nn}} is [[proximal]].

=====Inflection=====
{{Egyptian demonstratives}}

=====Alternative forms=====
{{egy-hieroforms
|M22*M22:n|read1=nn}}

===Etymology 2===
Oréal hypothesizes an origin in a contraction of {{af|egy|nj|pos1=negative particle|wnn|alt2=wn|t2=exists}}, following Vergote and rejecting an earlier hypothesis by Osing and Loprieno that would suggest an origin in {{af|egy|nj|pos1=negative particle|jn}}.<ref>Oréal, Elsa (2022) “The negative existential cycle in Ancient Egyptian” in Ljuba Veselinova & Arja Hamari (eds.), ''The Negative Existential Cycle'', Berlin: Language Science Press, pages 197–230</ref>

====Particle====
{{egy-part|proclitic|head=D35:n}}

# {{lb|egy|since Middle Egyptian|with a following noun or pronoun}} [[there is]] [[no]], [[there are]] no; {{ng|introduces an independent negated existential clause}}
#* {{Q|egy||ShS.|lines 99–101|quote={{egy-h|<!--99-->wa:a-A1-Z1-i-m-nb-m-a:k\-A-A24-ib*Z1:f-<!--100-->n&xt-A24-a*Z1:f-r-sn-n:nw-w-A1-Z1-Z1-f-!-D35:n-<!--101-->w-xA-A-nDs-A1-m-Hr:r-ib-s-n:Z2}}
|tr=wꜥ jm nb mꜥkꜣ jb.f nḫt ꜥ.f r snnw.f '''nn''' wḫꜣ m ḥr(j) jb.sn
