ḫr:
===Pronunciation===
{{egy-pr|q=preposition|o=χuɾ|m=χuʔ|ml=χuʔ|l=χøʔ}}

===Etymology 1===

====Preposition====
{{egy-prep|head=x:r}}

# in the [[presence]] of
# into the [[presence]] of, [[to]]
# by, through the choice or presence of

=====Usage notes=====
This preposition is used when the object is someone of higher status, such as a king or a god, relating one person to another when social customs prohibit specifying a direct relationship. Thus, one does not speak ‘to’ ({{m|egy|n}}) a god, but ‘in the presence of’ ({{m|egy||ḫr}}) him.

