ḫntj-jmntjw:
{{wp|Khenti-Amentiu}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|egy|ḫntj|gloss1=foremost|jmntjw|gloss2=westerners, i.e. the dead}}, plural of {{m|egy|jmntj||western(er)}}.

The word is first attested in the tombs of First Dynasty kings [[w:Den (pharaoh)|Den]] ({{m|egy|dn}}) and [[w:Qa'a|Qaa]] ({{m|egy|qꜣ-ꜥ}}), where it is associated with the dead kings. However, there is no certain evidence that it referred to a separate deity (rather than being an epithet for other deities) until the second half of the Fifth Dynasty.

===Pronunciation===
{{egy-pr}}

===Proper noun===
{{egy-proper noun|m|head=xnt-n:t*y-imnt-tyw-Z3}}

# [[foremost|Foremost]] of the [[westerner|Westerner]]s, an [[epithet]] used for various gods of the dead such as [[Osiris]] and [[Anubis]]
#* {{Q|egy||Amduat A II|First Hour, closing text, lines 7–8|quote={{egy-h|s-HD-D:ra-SPACE-SPACE-<!--8-->k:k:t-N2-z:r-q:Y2-k-H-st:t-tm-m-t:gb-pr-!-a:r-N31:k-SPACE-SPACE-m-r:n-k:n-r:a-ra*Z1:r-b-w-Xr:r-st:ir-xnt-n:t*y-imnt-tyw-N33B:N33B:N33B-A40}}
|tr=sḥḏ kk(w)t srq.k ḥtm(y)t (j)ꜥr.k m rn.k n(j) rꜥ r bw ẖr(j) wsjr '''ḫntj-jmntjw'''
|t=Brighten the darkness that you might make the Place of Destruction breathe, that you might ascend in your name of Ra to the place where Osiris, '''Foremost of the Westerners''', is.}}
# [[Khentiamentiu]], a [[god]] of the [[dead]] and [[patron]] god of the [[necropolis]] at [[Abydos]]

