# {{lb|egy|attached to a stative verb form}} [[he]], [[him]], [[they]], [[them]]

====Usage notes====
Some authors distinguish between the singular and plural as two different morphemes, treating plural {{m|egy||.w}} as a variant of Old Egyptian {{m|egy|.wy}} or {{m|egy|*.wj}} and singular {{m|egy||.w}} as a variant of Old Egyptian {{m|egy|.j}}; however, at least by Middle Egyptian, no distinction seems to have been made.

In Old Egyptian, {{m|egy||.w}} and its variants were used for the masculine plural, while {{m|egy|.tj}} and its variants were used for the feminine plural. By Middle Egyptian, {{m|egy||.w}} had taken on both roles, making plural {{m|egy|.tj}} rare.

This suffix is usually omitted entirely. When written at all, it is often written before the determinative of the verb.

