𓀁:
===Glyph origin===
This determinative was originally two separate signs, one with a seated man putting his hand to his mouth as a determinative for eating, and one where the seated man’s hand did not touch the mouth but was depicted palm-outward as a determinative for speech, intellect, and exclamations.<!--glyph A426?--> Later the latter sign was subsumed by the former. {{egy-hiero-color-men}}

<div>During the Heracleopolitan Period, confusion of this sign with the seated man {{egy-h|A1}} ({{m|egy|𓀀}}) resulted in the use of a variant of {{egy-h|A2}} with a ''standing'' man putting his hand to his mouth.<!--glyph A281? A456?--></div>

===Symbol===
