𓆱:
===Glyph origin===
Representing a [[trunk]] or [[branch]]. Old Kingdom examples show a tree trunk with all of its knots and branches lopped off but the one at the very end. Later New Kingdom examples instead depict a branch with twigs. The phonogrammatic value derives by the [[rebus principle]] from the glyph’s use as a logogram for {{m|egy|ḫt||wood}}.

===Symbol===
{{head|egy|symbol|head={{egy-h|xt}}|tr=ḫt}}

