# {{ng|[[logogram|Logogram]] for {{m|egy|sbꜣ||star}}.}}
# {{ng|[[logogram|Logogram]] for {{m|egy|wnwt||hour}}.}}
# {{ng|Used in {{egy-h|iaH:sbA}}, a [[logogram]] for {{m|egy|ꜣbd||month}}.}}
# {{ng|[[determinative|Determinative]] for stars and constellations, as in {{m|egy|sbꜣ||star}}, {{m|egy|msḫtjw||the Big Dipper, the Plough}}.}}
# {{ng|[[determinative|Determinative]] in {{m|egy|wnwt||hour}}.}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Gardiner|487}}
* {{R:egy:Betrò}}

𓇽:
===Glyph origin===
<div>Representing a star {{m|egy|𓇼}} ({{egy-h|dwA}}) in a circle, symbolically representing the world of the dead, which was in the oldest times associated with the places where the sun and stars reappeared after having been invisible.</div>

